  "$comment": "Extra Delight's oven, turned as the block faces. The block stays in the world: a small brick oven, open in front, its cavity x 4..12, y 2..9, z 4..14 over a base slab whose front (z 0..4, top at y 2) is a ledge. No door: the bakeware standing in the oven (a sheet, a tray, a pie dish...) slides out of the mouth onto the ledge for the cook and back in to bake. What bakes lies in it, drawn by the code: like things piled on each other, a pie's filling on its crust; the slots are the grid's places, unmarked: the tray is marked whole (row 0 at the back, column 0 on the cook's left). A click in the mouth above the bakeware pushes it back in or pulls it out. Its flat inner faces are lined with bricks; while the heat under the oven is on they glow from the floor up. While nobody uses it the scene shows the bakeware and what lies in it inside the oven.",
